            "guidance": "This skill is coherent with its description: it captures OpenClaw session files and archives full conversations to disk and provides local search and a local HTTP API. Before installing/running: \n\n- Understand it will persist full conversations (user messages, assistant replies, and any captured 'thought' content) to your filesystem—this can contain sensitive data. \n- The capture looks for session files under ~/.openclaw/sessions and writes to ~/.openclaw/workspace/memory by default; you can and should override --memory-dir to a controlled location or sandbox. \n- Automatic backup uses git commit + push if you configure a remote; do not set a remote you don't fully control (or keep auto_backup disabled) to avoid accidental exfiltration. Git pushes will use whatever system SSH/credentials are available. \n- The bundled REST API listens on 127.0.0.1:8765 by default (local only) — avoid exposing that port to untrusted networks. \n- The repository contains many executable scripts; inspect the code (or run in an isolated environment/container) before giving it access to real conversations. \n\nIf you want stronger assurance, ask for a focused review of the omitted files or run the test suite in an isolated environment; evidence of network calls to unexpected external endpoints or unconditional remote pushes would change the assessment to suspicious.",
